---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import { SITE, CTA_LABEL } from '../data/site';
import { PLANS, TRIAL_DAYS } from '../data/plans';
import { AVAILABLE_NETWORKS } from '../data/networks';
import { tool } from '../data/tools';
const [starter, team, pro, ultimate] = PLANS;
const available = AVAILABLE_NETWORKS.map((n) => n.name).join(', ');
// Monthly-billing rates for Buffer Essentials and Team, from src/data/tools/buffer.json.
const bufferTiers = tool('buffer').perChannel!.tiers;
const bufferRates = [bufferTiers.essentials[0][1], bufferTiers.team[0][1]];
const comparisons = [
  { href: '/compare/buffer', name: 'Buffer', text: `Buffer charges $${bufferRates[0]} to $${bufferRates[1]} per channel a month for the first ten channels and has a free plan for three channels. It is cheaper for one to three channels; PostDelegate’s flat plans cost less from five channels up.` },
  { href: '/compare/hootsuite', name: 'Hootsuite', text: 'Hootsuite is a full suite with an inbox and listening, from $99 per user a month. PostDelegate covers scheduling and approvals for a flat price, without the inbox.' },
  { href: '/compare/later', name: 'Later', text: 'Later is built for Instagram, TikTok and visual planning, with AI credits and post caps by plan. PostDelegate suits YouTube, Bluesky, blogs and newsletters today.' },
  { href: '/compare/sprout-social', name: 'Sprout Social', text: 'Sprout Social is a broad platform from $79 per seat a month, with its API on Advanced. PostDelegate includes the API and MCP on every plan.' },
  { href: '/compare/publer', name: 'Publer', text: 'Publer prices per account and member and has a free plan. It is cheaper for one or two accounts; PostDelegate keeps one flat price as you grow.' },
  { href: '/compare/post-bridge', name: 'Post Bridge', text: 'Questions to ask about channels, workflow and automation when choosing between two lighter publishing tools.' },
];
const faq = [
  { q: 'What is a cheaper alternative to Buffer?', a: `For five or more channels, PostDelegate usually costs less than Buffer: $${starter.monthly} a month for ${starter.channels} channels and $${team.monthly} for ${team.channels} channels with team members, where Buffer charges per channel. Check that the networks you need can connect today.` },
  { q: 'Which social media scheduler works with Claude or ChatGPT?', a: 'Several now do. PostDelegate has an MCP server on every plan, so Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, Claude Code and other MCP clients can draft and schedule posts, and drafts can wait in an AI review inbox for a person to approve. Buffer, Hootsuite and Publer also offer MCP connections, on different plans.' },
  { q: 'Can PostDelegate post to Instagram, Facebook, LinkedIn or TikTok?', a: `Not yet. Those networks, along with X, Threads and Pinterest, are coming soon and open as each platform approves PostDelegate. Today you can connect ${available}.` },
];
const crumbs = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'BreadcrumbList', itemListElement: [
  { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Compare', item: `${SITE.url}/compare` },
  { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Alternatives', item: `${SITE.url}/alternatives` }] };
const faqLd = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'FAQPage', mainEntity: faq.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })) };
---
<Doc title="Social media scheduler alternatives in 2026 — PostDelegate" description="Looking for a Buffer, Hootsuite, Later, Sprout Social or Publer alternative? Plain comparisons of pricing, trials, AI, API and the networks each connects." h1="Social media scheduler alternatives." eyebrow="Alternatives" lead="Comparing Buffer, Hootsuite, Later, Sprout Social and Publer with PostDelegate, including where each of them is the better pick today." jsonLd={[crumbs, faqLd]}>
  <a slot="actions" href={SITE.signup} class="button">{CTA_LABEL}</a>
  <a slot="actions" href="/pricing" class="button button-outline">See pricing</a>
  <h2>The comparisons</h2>
  <div class="document-grid">
    {comparisons.map((c) => <a href={c.href} class="document-card"><h3>PostDelegate vs {c.name}</h3><p>{c.text}</p><span>See the comparison →</span></a>)}
  </div>
  <h2>Alternatives to one tool</h2>
  <div class="document-grid">
    <a href="/alternatives/postiz" class="document-card"><h3>Postiz alternatives</h3><p>Hosted, self-hosted and API options compared by price, networks and MCP, including when to stay on Postiz.</p><span>See the alternatives →</span></a>
    <a href="/compare/postiz-vs-buffer" class="document-card"><h3>Postiz vs Buffer</h3><p>Worked monthly costs at 3, 10 and 30 accounts, with every price linked to its source.</p><span>See the comparison →</span></a>
  </div>
  <p>PostDelegate is built on the open-source Postiz project (AGPL-3.0). See <a href="/licenses">/licenses</a>.</p>
  <p>Competitor details on each page are taken from their own websites in October 2026. Plans change, so check each service’s website before you decide.</p>

  <h2>How to choose a scheduler</h2>
  <p>Most schedulers can put a post on a calendar. The differences that matter show up in four places. First, whether the exact accounts you manage can connect and publish today. Second, how the price is built: per channel, per account, per person or per plan, and what the total comes to for your real numbers. Third, how AI is paid for: an allowance or credits in the plan, or your own key. Fourth, how drafts get reviewed, by your team, your clients and any AI assistant that writes for you.</p>

  <h2>Who PostDelegate suits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Teams that work with AI assistants.</strong> The <a href="/mcp">MCP server</a> lets Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, Claude Code and other MCP clients draft and schedule posts on every plan. Drafts can wait in the AI review inbox until a person approves them. A public <a href="/api">REST API</a> and webhooks are included too.</li>
    <li><strong>Agencies that need client sign-off.</strong> Posts carry statuses, and clients approve posts from a link without creating an account. Customers keep each client’s channels together.</li>
    <li><strong>Anyone watching the budget.</strong> Plans are flat: ${starter.monthly} a month for {starter.channels} channels, ${team.monthly} for {team.channels} with team members, ${pro.monthly} for {pro.channels} and ${ultimate.monthly} for {ultimate.channels}. They are not priced per person, and AI runs on your own OpenAI API key, so PostDelegate never charges for AI.</li>
    <li><strong>Publishers beyond the big feeds.</strong> {AVAILABLE_NETWORKS.length} networks connect today: {available}.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who should look elsewhere for now</h2>
  <p>Instagram, Facebook, LinkedIn, TikTok, X, Threads and Pinterest are coming soon on PostDelegate, pending each platform’s approval, and cannot be connected yet. If one of those is your main channel, Buffer, Hootsuite, Later, Sprout Social or Publer will serve you better today. The same goes if you need a shared inbox for replying to comments and messages, or social listening, which PostDelegate does not offer.</p>

  <h2>Try it with your own content</h2>
  <p>Every PostDelegate plan starts with a {TRIAL_DAYS}-day free trial that needs no credit card. Connect an account you manage, prepare a representative post, send it for approval and schedule it. Then compare that with the trial of any service above.</p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <Faq items={faq} />
  <p>PostDelegate is operated independently by {SITE.operator} and is not affiliated with or endorsed by any of the services compared here. Their names belong to their owners.</p>
</Doc>
